I propose a second compromise based on:

- wraiths are the only reasonable way to get levels late in the game
- wraiths are easy to kill after a point

Make a creature that has a difficulty to kill proportional to the player's 
current level. When killed, it has a chance of leaving a corpse that can be
eaten to gain levels. Use this monster in the summoning by the bell instead of
wraiths. 

This also creates a monster that higher level characters would find a challenge.

I leave the details as an excercise for the reader. Answer may be printed from
the back of the book later.


